  "result": {
    "summary": "A Persian tactical victory and a Greek moral one. Xerxes forced the pass after the Anopaea path was betrayed, and the fleet withdrew from Artemisium; but the delay, the Persian losses and the example of the rearguard stiffened Greek resolve before Salamis and Plataea.",
    "casualties": {
      "A": "~1,500-2,000 killed in the rearguard (all 300 Spartans; ~700 Thespians); Thebans surrendered",
      "B": "Herodotus: up to 20,000; modern scholars far lower; two brothers of Xerxes (Abrocomes and Hyperanthes) among the dead"
    }
  },
